From: Magnus Reimann <magnus.reimann@mailbox.org>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 17:01:53 +0100
Subject: [PATCH gnumach 16/17] tests: add test-lll, check mutual exclusion of
 glibc-style low-level locks

Threads on all processors contend for locks built like glibc's Hurd
low-level locks (compare-and-swap fast path, exchange and gsync slow
path) and check that they are alone in the critical section.

* tests/test-lll.c: New file.
* tests/user-qemu.mk (USER_TESTS): Add tests/test-lll.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 tests/test-lll.c   | 182 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 tests/user-qemu.mk |   1 +
 2 files changed, 183 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 tests/test-lll.c

diff --git a/tests/test-lll.c b/tests/test-lll.c
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..01c72217
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/test-lll.c
@@ -0,0 +1,182 @@
